  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 243 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nReturn flow begins Saturday night as high pressure moves to the\neast of the state. Strong theta- e advection and an increasing \nlow level jet of 40-45 kts will lead to increasing instability \nand thunderstorm chances. \n\nUpper high pressure over Hudson Bay combined with upper high \npressure over the Four Corners region, will lead to progressive \nwesterly flow over much of the northern CONUS with periodic embedded \nshort waves passing across Iowa. This flow will also keep a surface \nboundary in the Midwest area and resulting in several chances for \nthunderstorms before Canadian high pressure arrives early next week. \nPWAT values of 1.50-2.00\" will be common during active storm periods \nthat could lead to an aggregate heavy rain threat through the week. \nTemperatures will be seasonal and mainly in the 80s through midweek \nthe gradual cooling as the Canadian high pressure approaches for the \nend of next week.",
